"""A reference of lab markers: what each one measures, and what values above or below the reference range can point to.

General education, not a diagnosis. A value outside the range is a prompt to ask a clinician, who reads it with the
person's history, medicines and the lab's own range. A lab result (by its marker name) is matched to an entry through
the same topics the monitoring match uses (see monitoring.py), so a LabCorp name like "Cholesterol, Total" or a
"Vitamin D, 25-Hydroxy" finds its entry whether it was picked from the list or kept as "Other"."""

import re

from app.labs.monitoring import result_topics

